#. +> trunk stable
#: kstars.kcfg:906
msgid "Place the observer above the specified longitude and latitude"
msgstr "Den Kieker op de angeven Längde un Breed stellen"

#. i18n: ectx: label, entry (XplanetLatitude), group (Xplanet)
#. i18n: ectx: property (toolTip), widget (KIntSpinBox, kcfg_XplanetLatitude)
#. +> trunk stable
#: kstars.kcfg:910 xplanet/opsxplanet.ui:767
msgid "Latitude in degrees"
msgstr "Geograafsch Breed, in Graad"

#. i18n: ectx: whatsthis, entry (XplanetLatitude), group (Xplanet)
#. i18n: ectx: property (whatsThis), widget (KIntSpinBox, kcfg_XplanetLatitude)
#. +> trunk stable
#: kstars.kcfg:911 xplanet/opsxplanet.ui:770
msgid ""
"Render the target body as seen from above the specified latitude (in "
"degrees).  The default value is 0."
msgstr ""
"Dat Teel so dorstellen, as Een dat vun de angeven Breed (in Graad) ankieken "
"dee. De Standardweert is \"0\"."

#. i18n: ectx: label, entry (XplanetLongitude), group (Xplanet)
#. i18n: ectx: property (toolTip), widget (KIntSpinBox, kcfg_XplanetLongitude)
#. +> trunk stable
#: kstars.kcfg:915 xplanet/opsxplanet.ui:790
msgid "Longitude in degrees"
msgstr "Geograafsch Längde, in Graad"

#. i18n: ectx: whatsthis, entry (XplanetLongitude), group (Xplanet)
#. +> trunk stable
#: kstars.kcfg:916
msgid ""
"Place the observer above the specified longitude (in degrees).  Longitude is "
"positive going east, negative going west (for the earth and moon), so for "
"example Los Angeles is at -118 or 242.  The default value is 0."
msgstr ""
"Den Kieker op de angeven Längde (in Graad) stellen. De Längde is Richt Oost "
"positiv, un na West negativ (för de Eer un den Maand). Jaad liggt a.B. op -8 "
"oder 352. De Standardweert is \"0\"."

#. i18n: ectx: label, entry (XplanetProjection), group (Xplanet)
